{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Words and music by Pat Songwriter","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Typically this type of credit is aligned to the right, so that the position information refers to the right-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most part of the text. But in this example, the text is center-justified, not right-justified.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The halign attribute is used in these situations. If it is not present, its value is the same as for the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"justify attribute. For elements where a justify attribute is not allowed, the default is implementation-"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"dependent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"halign","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/halign"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/halign"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV6halignAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"halign","symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/halign":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/halign","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/halign","title":"halign","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}